inframe browser models

This repository holds the three files the inframe web page downloads to run in the browser. They are converted
or copied, not trained here. Each keeps the license of its origin; the license texts are LICENSE-APACHE and
LICENSE-MIT in this repository, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES holds the notices of the libraries inside the .wasm file.

rfdetr_small_v1.onnx
  RF-DETR small (COCO checkpoint), exported to ONNX with rfdetr 1.5.2.
  Copyright Roboflow, Inc. Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE).
  Source: https://github.com/roboflow/rf-detr
  RF-DETR builds on LW-DETR, Deformable DETR, Conditional DETR and DINOv2 code and weights, which carry
  their own notices under the Apache License 2.0 in the source repository.

dinov2_s_v1.onnx
  DINOv2 small (facebook/dinov2-small), exported to ONNX (pooler_output, opset 17).
  Copyright Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE).
  Source: https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov2-small

ort-wasm-simd-threaded.asyncify.wasm
  ONNX Runtime Web 1.30.0 WebAssembly runtime (WebGPU build), unchanged.
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. MIT License (LICENSE-MIT) for the ONNX Runtime and MLAS code.
  The file is a statically linked binary and also contains third-party code, each under its own license:
    protobuf (Copyright 2008 Google Inc.)                    BSD-3-Clause
    abseil-cpp (Google)                                      Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE)
    onnx (Copyright Facebook, Inc. and Microsoft Corporation) Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE)
    Eigen                                                    MPL-2.0
    and smaller parts of nlohmann json (MIT), SafeInt (MIT), flatbuffers (Apache-2.0), re2 (BSD-3-Clause), XNNPACK (BSD-3-Clause).
  Their copyright notices and license texts are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, which must be kept with the file.
  Source: https://www.npmjs.com/package/onnxruntime-web (code: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime)

Changes: the two .onnx files are format conversions of the upstream weights (no retraining, fp32). The
.wasm file is the upstream file, byte for byte. manifest.json lists the size and sha256 of each file.
